From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: do not advertise monitor mode, which this build cannot run

Measured on the board, 2026-09-16:
- Stock image, NetworkManager managing wl0 (so its P2P device exists),
  wl0 down: `iw dev wl0 set type monitor` fails with -EIO and "Monitor+Data interface
  support (MON_DATA) disabled". The vendor guard in
  rwnx_cfg80211_change_iface() tests RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif) where the loop
  variable vif_el is meant, so any second vif refuses monitor mode.
- Same image with wl0 out of NetworkManager and a second managed vif wl1: the
  same refusal; with wl1 deleted (one vif):, the command succeeds.
- A test kernel whose guard counted only vifs the firmware has (not merged): with wl0 running and associated, `iw dev wl0 set type monitor`
  succeeded and within 155 ms rwnx_rxdataind_aicwf oopsed on a NULL pointer
  (rwnx_rx.c, skb_reset_tail_pointer(skb_monitor)); the rx thread
  aicwf_busrx_thr was gone afterwards and wl0 stayed at 4 received packets.

Code says (aic8800_fdrv/, compiled with CONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA, _MON_XMIT and
_MON_RXFILTER all n):
- rwnx_rxdataind_aicwf: a frame with RX_STAT_MONITOR plus another status bit
  takes a branch that copies only under CONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA, so skb_monitor
  stays NULL and is dereferenced. A failed skb_copy_expand() in the other
  branch ends the same way. That is the oops above.
- rwnx_netdev_monitor_ops sets ndo_start_xmit only under
  CONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT; the core calls it unchecked, so any packet still
  queued on a netdev switched to monitor jumps to address 0.
- rwnx_rx_sm_disconnect_ind reads rwnx_vif->drv_conn_state before its NULL
  check, and change_iface clears vif_table[] between remove_if and add_if
  while a disconnect indication for the old station can still arrive.
- Radiotap building hits BUG_ON for legacy rate indexes 4-7.
These are read from the code, not each reproduced; the oops is the one that
was measured. Fixing them is a series of its own, each needing its own proof.
- Advertised anyway: wiphy->interface_modes includes NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR,
  and the custchan module parameter, with custregd, narrows it to monitor only
  (rwnx_set_wiphy_params). The firmware's own MON_DATA capability is never
  read: rwnx_check_fw_hw_feature() is only called from inside #if 0.

What changes:
- NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR leaves interface_modes. cfg80211 then refuses a
  change to monitor (cfg80211_change_iface) and a new monitor interface
  (nl80211 new_interface, cfg80211_iftype_allowed) with -EOPNOTSUPP before
  the driver is called, so none of the paths above is reachable, in any vif
  combination, whether NetworkManager manages wl0 or not.
- custchan=1 is refused at wiphy setup with an error line. It sets
  rwnx_limits[0].types to MONITOR unconditionally, which with monitor gone from
  interface_modes makes wiphy_register() fail (wiphy_verify_combinations), and
  with custregd=1 it would also set interface_modes to monitor only.

Left as the vendor has it: the monitor code itself, the guard with the wrong
variable (now unreachable through cfg80211), and rwnx_interface_add()'s
monitor checks. Nothing calls rwnx_interface_add() with a monitor type in
this build (the initial monitor vif is under CONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA).

Falsifier, on the board (set type monitor on wl0), NetworkManager
running:
0. Image without this patch, wl0 unmanaged (one vif), wl0 down:
   `iw dev wl0 set type monitor` -> succeeds. Proves the path this closes.
   iw reports errors as "command failed: ... (-95)"; its exit code is not the
   errno (161 for -95, 251 for -5).
1. With this patch, NetworkManager managing wl0: `iw list` shows no monitor
   under "Supported interface modes"; `iw dev wl0 set type monitor` with wl0
   down and with wl0 up -> -EOPNOTSUPP (-95), no MON_DATA line, no oops.
2. With this patch, wl0 unmanaged (one vif), the arm that succeeded in 0:
   -> -EOPNOTSUPP.
3. `iw phy phy0 interface add mon0 type monitor` -> -EOPNOTSUPP, no mon0.
4. wl0 managed and up afterwards: associated, scan finds BSSes, traffic
   passes; dmesg has no oops and the rx thread aicwf_busrx_thr exists.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -8998,6 +8998,15 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+    /*
+     * NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR is not advertised. This build has neither
+     * CONFIG_RWNX_MON_DATA nor CONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT, and its monitor paths
+     * crash: the monitor netdev has no ndo_start_xmit, and a monitor frame
+     * that also carries another rx status dereferences a NULL skb in
+     * rwnx_rxdataind_aicwf. cfg80211 refuses a type the wiphy does not
+     * advertise before the driver is called (cfg80211_change_iface,
+     * nl80211 new_interface).
+     */
     wiphy->interface_modes =
     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)     |
     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)          |
@@ -9009,7 +9018,13 @@
     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_DEVICE)  |
     #endif
     #endif
-    BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR);
+    0;
+
+    /* custchan switches the wiphy to monitor-only, see above */
+    if (rwnx_mod_params.custchan) {
+        wiphy_err(wiphy, "custchan needs monitor mode, which this build does not support; ignored\n");
+        rwnx_mod_params.custchan = false;
+    }
 
 #if defined CONFIG_GPIO_WAKEUP || defined CONFIG_WOWLAN
 		/* Set WoWLAN flags */
